    {
      "finding": "The first palette-aware fixture omitted scheme, leaving apply_qpalette at its default dark palette.",
      "correction": "2a64bc3bcee4d96aa4ea12561fac2cc34cbceab1",
      "validation": "The sole fixture argument was corrected; six affected existing assertions passed2.38s on explicit dark/light/high_contrast palettes. Product bytes stayed unchanged."
    }
  ],
  "source_review": [
    "Only private _Well focus/cache/paint methods and required imports change. Existing mouse/drag/selection, checked state, geometry, public docs/captions and alpha visibility remain unchanged.",
    "Ordinary focus uses actual palette highlight/highlighted-text roles. Strong focus keeps the existing shared theme colour except when its contrast against the selected fixed CHOSEN fill is below the existing threshold; only then a local cached black/white fallback is selected.",
    "Empty well styling and a passing high-contrast selected ring retain their generic colours. Selected centers stay blue, both states preserve fixed well size, and the outline is overlaid after normal button painting.",
    "The cache refreshes on style/palette/application font changes; no preference lookup or contrast computation occurs during paint. Focus entry/exit requests repaint and calls the normal base implementation.",
    "Actual normal policy excludes all five added private declarations, helper inventory semantics unchanged; only original nested helper line offsets move."
  ],
  "recorded_validation": {
    "original": "All3themes reproduced invisible focused/unfocused state while Tab/Space/name already worked.",
    "owning": "45 passed7.21s includes37 existing selection/mouse/drag cases; this predates the exact palette argument correction.",
    "final_affected": "6 passed,2 deselected2.38s with explicit3theme palettes; unchanged actual rendered contrast/uniform3px/center/fill/geometry/livepreference assertions.",
    "do_not_sum_overlapping_runs": true
  },
